   "title": "Share of kept edits that were not truly better, by keep rule",
   "takeaway": "Under 'strictly better on one noisy number', 19% [16, 22] of keeps had no true gain (same for the upstream default), vs 4.6% under the rigor rule and 1% under a noise-band gate. Rigor cuts the optimism gap from 0.0041 to 0.0015 but tests about 25% fewer ideas (112 vs 149), so its true final is slightly worse (0.958 vs 0.956, lower is better). On real tiny-LM runs (3 seeds) the ordering was not resolved.",
